---
title: "Last writer wins on Lamport stamps: B never saw milk, which is lost"
---
sequenceDiagram
    participant L0 as A
    participant L1 as B
    Note over L0: write milk<br/>L 1<br/>x (1,A)→"milk"
    Note over L1: local<br/>L 1<br/>x (empty)
    Note over L1: local<br/>L 2<br/>x (empty)
    Note over L1: write eggs<br/>L 3<br/>x (3,B)→"eggs"
    Note over L0,L1: milk is concurrent with eggs: B never heard from A. Yet the stamps are the same as when B saw milk, (1,A) and (3,B), so nothing in them can tell
    L1->>L0: (3,B)→"eggs"
    Note over L0: sync<br/>L 4<br/>x (3,B)→"eggs"
    Note over L1,L0: A drops "milk" for "eggs" and ends exactly as when B saw milk: no one chose to discard "milk", and nothing on either replica records it was written
